Z||000000||Sevaan||02-22-2001||07:45 PM||||Hey everyone,<P>I just bought my own Fiero yesterday. It's a silver 1986 2m4, and I got it for $1500 Canadian. It's an automatic.<P>It's in pretty good condition, but there are a few issues.<P>Namely, the clutch seems to hold on to the gear too long before changing...so what happens is that I'll be driving, and the gear needs to change, and instead of changing my foot is just reving the engine, then suddenly it engages.<P>What do you think the problem is? This weekend I will probably check the spark plugs and stuff.<P>And this is my first car, and I don't really know too much about 'em (I bought an old car so it would be a good learning experience). If you have any tips and tricks for the Fiero, I'd really appreciate it.<P>It's a very cool car, and I'm quite happy with it!||||reg||10
Z||000001||Sevaan||02-22-2001||07:49 PM||||Oh yeah, it came with new brakes, timing chain, some wiring stuff, and a clutch (so I don't think that's going).||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GT||02-22-2001||07:54 PM||||I recently drove a 88GT that had the same problem.  Car couldnt even get up a little incline when the clutch was released.  It would catch a little then go.  Next thing I knew, the clutch starting burning and smoke was going everywhere.  The clutch was shot in my case.  Sounds like yours is pretty similar situation.. I could be wrong.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sevaan||02-22-2001||07:57 PM||||Well it's driving fine up hills, down, etc. But it just revs a lot between gear changes. Not all the time, mind you, but enough for me to notice.<p>[This message has been edited by Sevaan (edited 02-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GT||02-22-2001||08:03 PM||||I could drive this 88 around the yard and all but going up that cline it would just rev real loud and wouldnt go, then I saw the smoke.  Burnt clutch smell is something you dont forget either.  Glad to hear you like your 2M4 though.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||02-22-2001||08:11 PM||||Low transmission fluid?  May need some transmission service for automatics.  New gaskets and filter.  Drain and flush transmission.  Something is slipping, not a good sign.<P>Expensive to replace an automatic transmission.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||02-22-2001||08:47 PM||||<A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A> read the TH125 article. should give you a starting place.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Sevaan||02-22-2001||09:05 PM||||I bought it yesterday, and today took it to a lube place and replaced everything. Hopefully it will help.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroJoe||02-22-2001||09:23 PM||||Welcome to the wonderful world of Fiero ownership!<P>We'd all like to see your car!  If you can, post some pics in the "General Fiero Chat" section of this forum.  To post a picture, click on the "Pennock's Image Poster" icon at the bottom of any forum page.  Download the software, follow its instructions, and away you go!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||daved||02-22-2001||10:14 PM||||New clutch in an automatic! Hmmmmm. Think they sold you a line there.<BR>There could be two causes that are easily fixable in an automatic.<BR>1.  Change the filter inside the tranny.<BR>2.  Adjust the TV cable. (its attached to part of the throttle mechanism)<P>You might try buying the Haynes manual from Canadian Tire #25-9303-8 at $17 each is a good investment. Or try Ogres Cave.<BR>Good luck,  Dave ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Sevaan||02-22-2001||10:22 PM||||Not new clutch! My bad. New transmission, I mean.<P>As I said, I don't know much about cars.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||02-22-2001||11:01 PM||||Does the Fiero automatic tranny use a vacuum modulator like the old GM TurboHydramatic trannies?  A vacuum leak on one will cause it to hold the gear longer because it thinks you're into the throttle heavier.  Had that problem on my old 72 T/A with a TH400 tranny.  New vacuum hose fixed everything.||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||02-22-2001||11:51 PM||||TH125 uses a TV cable only. One of the 4 speeds uses a TV cable and a vac mod. The newer 4 speeds are electric.||||reg||1
